.TH CCOL_ITER_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_iter_destroy \- destroy a unified iterator before the end
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <citerators.h>   /* or any container header */

ccol_iter_destroy(it);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Destroys the iterator by calling its own _free_fn callback and sets it
to NULL.  Must be called when breaking out of a manual for loop before
the iterator reaches NULL naturally.

When using ccol_iter_declare(), RAII cleanup handles destruction
automatically on scope exit; ccol_iter_destroy() is only necessary
when you need to release resources before the end of the scope.
Inside ccol_for_each(), the iterator is always destroyed on exit.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
it   Iterator variable declared with ccol_iter_declare().
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call when it is already NULL (no-op).
After this call, it is NULL and must not be used again.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_iter_declare (3),
.BR ccol_iter_next (3),
.BR ccol_for_each (3)
